This being only my third ascension and the first try with a "non-easy"
class (Rogue), I expected and got a challenge; twenty-five deaths is
too many to learn to play defensively.  However, attempt #26 turned out
to be quite easy.  Nothing warms the heart like being on level 2 of
Sokoban and seeing these messages:

n - an oak wand
What do you want to write with? [- n or ?*] n
You may wish for an object.--More--

This was the first of three wands of wishing I found (including the
castle wand).  As a result, I found the ascension rather unexciting,
but still a good learning experience on how not to rely on melee
combat.

- Learned how to use missile weapons and Elbereth in combination,
though I often found myself running out of ammo due to weight
restrictions early on (need to keep playing "weak" characters nad find
a better balance between armor and weapon weight).
- Did Sokoban first, found /oW #1, wished up 2b?oC, GDSM, gauntlets of
power, and boots of jumping.  Sokoban had an amulet of reflection, so
wished up a bag of holding--turned out to be a good plan because I
never found a bag or sack anywhere.
- Returned to the mines, found a luckstone in a bones pile, and picked
up a second at Mine's End.
- Back to the dungeons... found a number of shrines to buy protection,
converted a random altar for a stash point on DL15, and found /oW #2 on
DL18.  Wished up the cloak of displacement, two magic markers, helm of
telepathy, and a T-shirt with the wrested charge.
- Received crowning/Stormbringer by accident while sacrificing the
prayer timeout away to make some holy water.
- Crushed the quest, Medusa, and Castle at XL17-ish to pick up /oW #3.
Given how nice the RNG had been so far, I asked for a couple of magic
markers and stashed the wand for the ascension run.
- Visited Ludios to get more cash for protection.  Got 2 more wishes
from the throne there; tried and failed for Grayswandir, then asked for
another magic marker.
- Major mistake #1: I forgot to put on the ring of levitation while
re-crossing Croesus's moat.  Lost the helm, but fortunately my bag of
holding protected its contents well.  Broke out /oW #3 for an amulet of
magical breathing, retrieved the helm, recharged the wand, and really
stashed it this time.
- Major mistake #2: Lazily meleeing disenchanters.  Wasted a number of
enchantment points that way.
- Levelled up to 27 by reverse genociding wraiths. (Quaffed 3 potions
of gain level on Astral.)
- Claimed the candelabrum, book, and the Amulet with conflict and a
conveniently spawned rubber chicken. (The High Priest of Moloch is
slowing down...)
- Quick jaunt to Astral.  Left altar with Famine was no good, but the
center altar with Death did the trick.

